WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:07.999
Ally stared at the diner entrance. "Why are humans so complicated?" she thought.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.760
"If they could read minds like Astralians, I wouldn't have to explain things to Bethany—she'd already know the truth!"

3
00:00:18.761 --> 00:00:24.244
"What's the matter, hon?" Flo asked. "Is something bothering you?"

4
00:00:24.245 --> 00:00:25.496
"There is. I—"

5
00:00:25.497 --> 00:00:31.900
"Tonight's going to be epic!" Barry cried, bursting into the diner.

6
00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:38.478
Ally scowled at him. "I know you wanted to try out the plate levitation trick tonight, Barry.

7
00:00:38.479 --> 00:00:43.494
But please don't. This night is too important to Ray."

8
00:00:43.495 --> 00:00:46.879
Barry gave her a thumbs-up. "Got it."

9
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.232
"Go on, Ally," Flo said. "What were you saying?"

10
00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:56.878
Ally didn't want to talk about her problems in front of Barry, but she needed advice about Bethany.

11
00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:00.486
"I know! I'll ask Alpha!" Ally thought.

12
00:01:00.487 --> 00:01:10.723
"It's nothing, Flo, thanks," Ally said. "I'm going to fix my hair before the gala begins."

13
00:01:10.724 --> 00:01:14.237
*** Ally ducked into the restroom and reached into her apron

14
00:01:14.238 --> 00:01:19.381
pocket. But Alpha wasn't there! Ally checked

15
00:01:19.382 --> 00:01:23.057
everywhere. She checked the floor under the sink and next to the

16
00:01:23.058 --> 00:01:25.643
toilet. Alpha was gone.

17
00:01:25.644 --> 00:01:30.511
Again! "Maybe I dropped her in the dining room!" Ally raced out of the restroom to search for Alpha.

18
00:01:30.512 --> 00:01:33.974
But the gala guests had begun to arrive.

19
00:01:33.975 --> 00:01:36.825
There was no way Ally could search for Alpha now.

20
00:01:36.826 --> 00:01:43.562
"I can't even listen for Alpha's strange noises because I powered her down," she thought. "Now what?"

21
00:01:43.563 --> 00:01:49.496
"Ally!" Randy waved her into the kitchen and handed her a tray of appetizers.

22
00:01:49.497 --> 00:01:55.479
"Pass around these Cosmic Crescents. They're puff pastry filled with spinach and cheese."

23
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:59.979
Ally knew the gala was very important to Ray; it needed to go perfectly.

24
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.723
But she was having a hard time keeping her mind on her job.

25
00:02:03.724 --> 00:02:10.240
As she wound her way through the guests, passing out food, she sneaked peeks under tables and in corners.

26
00:02:10.241 --> 00:02:14.587
"Alpha has to be somewhere in the diner," Ally thought.

27
00:02:14.588 --> 00:02:19.911
Once the tray of Cosmic Crescents was empty, Ally went back to the kitchen for another tray.

28
00:02:19.912 --> 00:02:23.517
"These are Spinning Suns," Randy said.

29
00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:32.151
"They're mini pizzas with cheese and yellow peppers. Please tell people to be careful—they're hot."

30
00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:37.224
Ally had just begun to pass out the Spinning Suns when something underneath a table caught her eye.

31
00:02:37.225 --> 00:02:41.142
It was small and shiny—just like the device!

32
00:02:41.143 --> 00:02:44.639
Still holding the tray, Ally rushed across the diner.

33
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.853
But she was so focused on the object under the table, she wasn't looking where she was going.

34
00:02:49.854 --> 00:02:56.771
Boom! She slammed into a tall gentleman who'd just entered the diner, and the tray of hot Spinning Suns flew out of her hand.

35
00:02:56.772 --> 00:03:02.018
Ally quickly activated her levitation powers and stopped the tray just before it hit the floor.

36
00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:07.088
She grabbed the tray and turned to him. "Sorry, sir. I didn't see you there."

37
00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:10.671
The man smiled. "That was amazing, young lady!

38
00:03:10.672 --> 00:03:14.316
I've heard such wonderful things about your tricks.

39
00:03:14.317 --> 00:03:23.776
So when the League of Rocket Scientists invited me to be their keynote speaker, I knew I had to come tonight."

40
00:03:23.777 --> 00:03:31.574
"He's the president!" Ally thought as the man walked away. "And that was a close call!"

41
00:03:31.575 --> 00:03:34.775
She quickly glanced under the table to look for Alpha.

42
00:03:34.776 --> 00:03:42.560
"Ugh," she thought. The shiny object was someone's phone, not the device.

43
00:03:42.561 --> 00:03:48.997
*** While the guests ate and the president gave his speech, Ally took every chance she had to look for Alpha.

44
00:03:48.998 --> 00:03:54.411
"I can't believe I lost her a second time," Ally scolded herself.

45
00:03:54.412 --> 00:03:59.437
"I'm glad my parents aren't here—they'd be so disappointed in me."

46
00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:04.392
"Ally, it's almost time to present Randy's rocket ship cake," Flo said.

47
00:04:04.393 --> 00:04:10.902
"As soon as the president finishes his speech, you can carry it out."

48
00:04:10.903 --> 00:04:17.395
Ally went into the kitchen to get the cake, but Barry was already carrying the elaborately decorated cake.

49
00:04:17.396 --> 00:04:22.947
"Be careful," Ally warned. "No tricks."

50
00:04:22.948 --> 00:04:27.895
"Don't worry," Barry said. "This is going to be perfect!"

51
00:04:27.896 --> 00:04:34.176
As soon as Barry stepped into the dining room with the rocket ship cake, the guests exploded into applause.

52
00:04:34.177 --> 00:04:38.341
"That looks so real," one said.

53
00:04:38.342 --> 00:04:41.629
"I can't believe we can eat that!" another said.

54
00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.932
Ally held her breath as Barry made it all the way across the dining room with the cake.

55
00:04:45.933 --> 00:04:49.849
He was just about to set it down in front of the president when he tripped.

56
00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:55.121
The cake flew up—and landed right in the president's lap!

57
00:04:55.122 --> 00:05:04.826
The room went silent as Barry stood there looking shocked, a broken spring dangling from his finger.

